#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Clean NIFTY minute-by-minute straddle simulator.

Design:
    C++ decoder :9001
            |
            v
    one normalized live market book
            |
            +--> 09:16 engine
            +--> 09:17 engine
            +--> 09:18 engine
            +--> 09:19 engine
            +--> NOW engine

Important:
- This file is independent from the legacy simulation_server.py.
- It does not load LUTs.
- It does not load the GammaShortDaily reference file.
- It does not use the old five-stage signal engine.
- It keeps independent state for every run.
- START NOW builds immediately from the current complete live chain.
- Every active run records one minute snapshot at most once per wall-clock minute.

Quote policy:
The current C++ feed seen during debugging was producing invalid bid/ask values
(e.g. CE bid=0 and ask=5242.88 for a ~24150 ATM option). Therefore this clean
simulator deliberately uses LTP for simulated entry/exit marking when the
bid/ask pair fails sanity checks. It reports quote_source=LTP_FALLBACK rather
than pretending the bad bid/ask are executable prices.

Once the C++ top-of-book parser is corrected, set USE_LTP_FALLBACK=False to
require a valid bid/ask pair.
"""

